<!-- Website teaching layer; original sync-vs-async.md remains unchanged. Primary-source review: batch-1.json. -->
<!-- @opening -->
<p class="story-lead">The profile request is inside a suspend function, yet the screen still freezes. That function called a blocking client on the main thread. The keyword permitted suspension; the called operation never used it.</p>

Inspect two contracts separately: how the caller receives completion, and what the executing thread does while waiting. A non-blocking client and blocking I/O moved to a worker can both protect the UI thread, but their waiting-resource costs differ.

<!-- @after First Principles :: animation -->
### Follow the task and the thread separately

<section class="pb-figure" data-pb-flow="scene" aria-label="Same remote wait, different thread occupancy">
